Viewer: moving the music onto the song's timeline no longer leaves a gap; music counters in the viewer log (2026-10-12).

On the F50 the music still broke off for about a second now and then: each new song the element was moved
onto the song's timeline by dropping what was buffered, which was a moment of silence and then no cushion
for the next Wi-Fi gap. The last 5 s of fragments are now kept; a realignment empties the buffer and appends
the audio not heard yet again on the new timeline, with the sample being heard at that moment as the song
position. Desktop Chrome, 400 ms Wi-Fi gap every 3 s and a new song every 6 s, over 21 s: 1.6 s of waiting
before, 3 ms after; the element runs 0.06 s behind the song instead of 0.46 s. The viewer log now counts the
element's waits, skips ahead and realignments (musicWaits, musicSkips, musicAligns).

